{
  "_meta": {
    "title": "roman-numeral element lores: the +10 upstream misses (#887)",
    "source": "DDO Wiki, read 2026-10-16 through the in-app Browser pane: every member of the 45 `Category:<Element> Lore <roman> items` categories Template:Spelllore files (the 9 `Spell Lore` ones are the +0 case and are excluded).",
    "rule": "A roman-numeral magnitude on an ELEMENT lore is Roman2Dec(numeral) + 10; on universal Spell Lore it is the numeral. Stated three independent ways: Template:Spelllore's coding (`Roman2Dec + {{#ifeq:..spell..0~10}}`), the Spell Lore article's table ('Spell Lore enchantment comes in different strengths, marked with a Roman numeral': I-XII = <Type> Lore 11%-22%, Spell Lore 1%-12%), and rendered tooltips (Pale Rod 'Void Lore VI: ... 16%', Epic Halcyonia 'Healing Lore X: ... 20%', Brine Shaman's Staff 'Ice Lore I: ... 11%'). See docs/wiki-evidence/spell-lore.md.",
    "upstream": "gear-planner c36b45e reads every one of these as the bare numeral (Void Lore VI -> 6). src/roman_lore.py raises each by 10 and FAILS THE BUILD unless the record still holds exactly `from`, so the day upstream fixes its parser every entry goes stale loudly and is deleted rather than double-applied.",
    "shape": "`items`: record name -> entries {stat (canonical, post name-correction), numeral, from, to, category}. Also applied to the record's `[Upgraded]` twin (#879), which copies the base's affixes. `no_catalog_affix`: page lores with no affix on the record to correct — recorded, never added. `not_in_catalog`: member pages with no catalog record. `handled_elsewhere`: lores already corrected by another mechanism."
  },
